    "created_at": "2023-02-12T21:59:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-12T22:21:47Z",
    "body": "> But HTML does not specify that the prototype of {Dedicated,Shared}WorkerGlobalScope instances cannot change.\r\n\r\nIt shouldn’t need to, right? As you mentioned, Web IDL covers this. Perhaps a note would be helpful in HTML though?\r\n\r\nHTML needs to define [[SetPrototypeOf]] for WindowProxy because that object doesn’t implement the Window interface in the Web IDL sense. Unlike Web IDL [Global] interface instances, a WindowProxy’s observed prototype is only “immutable” in a user-code-cannot-change-it-directly sense. Its reported prototype can differ between invocations: it returns `null` for cross-origin access and otherwise returns `this.[[Window]].[[GetPrototypeOf]]()`. Because `this.[[Window]]` (the real Web IDL interface instance) can change, observed non-null prototypes for it can change over time too.\r\n\r\nSince there’s no “WorkerProxy” indirection layer in worker environments, Web IDL’s [Global] already fully defines their GPO/SPO behavior; their global objects === their global this ... uh ... global thisses? (global these? 🤔 _global theses...?_)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
