    "created_at": "2023-02-12T23:23:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-12T23:32:10Z",
    "body": "> It shouldn’t need to, right? As you mentioned, Web IDL covers this. Perhaps a note would be helpful in HTML though?\r\n\r\nAccording to WebIDL, any prototype in the prototype chain of a global can't have its prototype changed. Note that we're talking about an interface's prototype object. WebIDL does not talk about whether the global object can have its prototype changed. HTML does talk about it for `WindowProxy` instances, but not for worker global objects.\r\n\r\n```js\r\nObject.setPrototypeOf(window, {});  // Forbidden by HTML\r\nObject.setPrototypeOf(Window.prototype, {});  // Forbidden by WebIDL\r\n```\r\n\r\nI don't think the difference between `Window` and `WindowProxy` matters here.",
